### Limit menu-character suppression to shelf digits

**Severity:** `medium`

The unconditional `WM_MENUCHAR` branch closes mnemonic processing for every character, not just the new shelf shortcuts. That can suppress normal Alt-letter access keys elsewhere in the window. Restrict the workaround to the numeric access keys owned by the shelf so other mnemonics continue through normal window processing.

```suggestion
            // Suppress the system chime for the shelf's Alt+0 through Alt+9 access keys,
            // while preserving the normal handling of other window mnemonics.
            case PInvoke.WM_MENUCHAR when (wParam.Value & 0xFFFF) is >= (nuint)'0' and <= (nuint)'9':
                return (LRESULT)(1 << 16); // MAKELRESULT(0, MNC_CLOSE)
```

### Let the focused filter keep its Alt+Down shortcut

**Severity:** `medium`

This shell-level preview handler runs before the focused filter dropdown receives its existing Alt+Down command. In collapsed compact mode, the shell therefore expands the palette instead of opening the filter. Detect events originating within `FiltersDropDown` and route them through the existing child/default handling before claiming the chord for compact expansion.

```suggestion
            case VirtualKey.Down when modifiers.OnlyAlt:
                {
                    var source = e.OriginalSource as DependencyObject;
                    while (source is not null && !ReferenceEquals(source, shellPage.FiltersDropDown))
                    {
                        source = Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Media.VisualTreeHelper.GetParent(source);
                    }

                    if (source is not null)
                    {
                        goto default;
                    }

                    if (shellPage.TryExpandCollapsedCompact())
                    {
                        e.Handled = true;
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // Outside collapsed compact mode, Alt+Down remains available to requested
                        // command keybindings just like every other unreserved chord.
                        goto default;
                    }

                    break;
                }
```
